  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows increasing negativity.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes by applying a 10-15% dampening factor to the immediate next period.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above 30-day moving average, reduce by 5-10% in subsequent periods.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0) to avoid underestimating rebound potential.",
    "Correct for lagged response: if true outcome is significantly higher than forecast 2-3 days later, adjust future forecasts upward by 2-5% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00), use historical volatility-weighted smoothing to avoid overconfidence in short-term trends."
  ]
}
